{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790979899,"nonce":"6qo0lb8mCK6LLpBAQmNm/bNT05M=","title":"Native ash cannot run haxe.zip.Compress without an fmt.hdll on disk","message":"std/src/fmt.rs implements fmt's digests and zlib streams. They are only wired in for sandbox targets (`sandbox_primitive`, `#[cfg(not(any(unix, windows)))]`). A native ash program that reaches `haxe.zip.Compress` / `Uncompress` (or `haxe.crypto.Md5` etc.) looks for `fmt.hdll` beside the program. With none there, it refuses to start:\n\n```\nError: Required library 'fmt' not found in \"\u003cprogram dir\u003e\"\n```\n\nStock HashLink ships fmt.hdll next to `hl`, so the same program runs there. ash has no fmt.hdll of its own to stage, so on ash these std classes are unusable unless the user copies HashLink's in.\n\n**Reproducer:**\n```haxe\nclass Z { static function main() {\n\tvar b = haxe.io.Bytes.alloc(100000); for (i in 0...b.length) b.set(i, i % 7);\n\tvar c = haxe.zip.Compress.run(b, 6);\n\tSys.println('compressed ${b.length} -\u003e ${c.length}, roundtrip ${haxe.zip.Uncompress.run(c).compare(b) == 0}');\n} }\n```\n`haxe -main Z -hl z.hl \u0026\u0026 ash $PWD/z.hl` in an empty directory. Expected: it prints and round-trips. Actual: the error above, before `main` runs.\n\n**Ask:** on native targets, fall back to the built-in fmt primitives when no fmt.hdll is found. A real fmt.hdll still wins, since it carries image and audio decoding.\n\n**Who needs it:** ashui's snapshot tool writes PNGs with an uncompressed (stored) deflate for lack of this. With it, `haxe.zip.Compress` is the whole encoder, and the same code runs on stock HashLink.","files":null}]}